			"notes": {
				"rationale": "unter keinen Umständen is an idiom Duden lists under Umstand, a Locution ADV with no comparison forms, like auf keinen Fall (de/idiom). keinen is a fixed member (de/fixed-member-test): allen in its slot gives unter allen Umständen, a different idiom with the opposite meaning, and diesen makes the phrase compositional. So a click on any of the three words selects the whole Locution (de/largest-fixed-unit), and keinen has no DET target of its own (de/locutions-and-sayings-are-made-of-lexemes). The Canonical Form is Duden's headword, lowercase unter despite the sentence-initial Unter (de/canonical-form-is-the-headword). Ruled 2026-10-02 (#701, grouping audit Q3)."
